{
  "$comment": "gosleep hooks. Stop[0] = the owner's turn-must-end-with-text guard (GSL-82) — do not weaken. Everything else = the T1 event layer (GSL-83): tools/lab/lab-log.sh normalizes each hook payload into docs/lab/events/YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl. 0 tokens, no model cooperation. lab-log.sh is fail-open (always exits 0), so a broken event layer can never wedge a session. Hooks are NOT snapshotted — a file watcher reloads this file mid-session, so an edit here hits the LIVE fleet: validate with `jq .` and verify with a real run (tools/lab/hooks-verify.sh).",
  "hooks": {
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/stop-require-final-text.sh",
            "timeout": 10,
            "statusMessage": "Проверка: ход заканчивается текстом владельцу"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/lab-log-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/lab-log-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionEnd": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/lab-log-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SubagentStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/lab-log-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SubagentStop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/lab-log-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "TeammateIdle": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/lab-log-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "StopFailure": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/lab-log-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreCompact": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/lab-log-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostCompact": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/lab-log-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "TaskCreated": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/lab-log-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "TaskCompleted": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/lab-log-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Notification": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/lab-log-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "$comment": "ONE hook, no `if`. The `if` field exists (v2.1.85+) and would pre-filter before spawning the process — but a real run on 2.1.207 showed two `if` rules under one matcher BOTH firing on the same call (one action -> two events), and `Bash(git *)` matching a command that only MENTIONED git inside a quoted string. Routing by sub-command prefix inside lab-log.sh is the version we can prove correct; the cost is one process spawn per Bash call.",
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/lab-log-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 },
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/chronicler-debounce-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      },
      {
        "$comment": "Second command = GSL-198: the debounce trigger from the ORIGINAL design (05-lab-ui-mobile-autonomy.md:184 — 'a PostToolUse async hook debounced on writes to docs/lab/') that fell out at implementation. The shim arms a background waiter and exits instantly; the chronicler runs once per quiet window. Kill switch: GOSLEEP_DEBOUNCE_DISABLE=1. Runbook: docs/runbooks/tick-engine.md.",
        "matcher": "Write|Edit|MultiEdit",
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/lab-log-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 },
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/chronicler-debounce-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "mcp__atlassian__.*",
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/tools/hooks/lab-log-hook.sh", "timeout": 5 }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
